{"stage": "step:s1", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2473, "output_tokens": 587, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "I recorded the key figures for step s1. Sensor-T2 is the best on unirradiated resolution but fails the hard efficiency requirement, so it is ruled out.\n\n**Documents read:** `candidate_specs.md`, `irradiation_testbeam_2026.md`, `simulation_summary_2025.md`, and `meeting_notes_2026-03-02.md`. The candidate spec gives only qualitative descriptions and no thickness options or numbers, so the figures below come from the other documents.\n\n| Technology | Hit efficiency at 2e16 neq/cm\u00b2 | Meets \u226597%? | Single-hit resolution (2025 sim, 150 \u00b5m, unirradiated) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Sensor-T1 (planar, standard pitch) | 98.5% | Yes | 9.0 \u00b5m |\n| Sensor-T2 (thin-pitch, large charge sharing) | 82.0% | **No** (strong charge trapping) | 6.0 \u00b5m |\n| Sensor-T3 (3D electrodes, larger pitch) | 99.2% | Yes | 14.0 \u00b5m |\n\n- The requirement is \u226597% efficiency up to 2e16 neq/cm\u00b2, and this is a hard constraint.\n- No thickness options beyond the 50\u2013300 \u00b5m range in the brief were found in the documents.\n- The resolution figures are from a single 2025 study at 150 \u00b5m and unirradiated. They are not yet the post-irradiation or thickness-optimised values.\n\n**Next step implied:** among the two technologies that pass the efficiency requirement, Sensor-T1 has the better resolution at 150 \u00b5m (9.0 \u00b5m vs 14.0 \u00b5m for Sensor-T3). I'd expect the thickness scan to decide the final choice.", "type": "text"}]}
